.title = "Argument Parsing",
.date = "2026-09-28",
.author = "ZigCC",
.layout = "section.shtml",
---

Command line arguments are available through `std.process.Init`. This small parser walks through
them once and recognizes one flag, one option with a value, and positional arguments.

It uses only Zig's standard library, so the parsing logic is visible instead of hidden behind a
package. The fixed-size file list also keeps memory ownership simple.

